# Every text file is LF in the repo and in the working tree, whatever the
# machine's core.autocrlf (Git for Windows sets it to true system-wide).
# Pharo writes LF, and the runner suite compares program output to .expected
# files byte for byte.
*           text=auto eol=lf

# Windows batch files need CRLF for cmd.exe to handle labels and goto reliably.
*.bat       text eol=crlf

# Pharo's own files, should any ever be added.
*.image     binary
*.changes   binary
*.sources   binary
*.zip       binary
